        "surveyID": "110036",
        "surveySubType": "Population Assessment",
        "narrative": "<p>LAKE TROUT ABUNDANCE HAS APPARENTLY DECLINED SINCE THE INITIAL SURVEY CONDUCTED IN 1978. AVERAGE SIZE OF LAKE TROUT APPEARS TO BE ABOUT THE SAME. THE LAKE TROUT POPULATION IS NATURALLY REPRODUCING, AND SEVERAL YEAR CLASSES WERE REPRE- SENTED IN THE SMALL SAMPLE OBTAINED. WALLEYE ABUNDANCE HAS ALSO DECLINED SIGHIFICANTLY SINCE 1978. YEAR-CLASS REPRESENTATION IS SPOTTY, BUT THE SAMPLE SIZE IN THIS ASSESSMENT IS SMALL. WALLEYE GROWTH IS GOOD BUT STILL BELOW STATE AVERAGE. BURBOT ARE ABUNDANT, AND THEIR NUMBERS SEEM TO HAVE INCREASED SINCE 1978. WHITEFISH CONTINUE TO BE VERY ABUNDANT, WITH GOOD AVERAGE SIZE. NORTHERN CISCO WERE TAKEN IN THIS ASSESSMENT AFTER BEING MISSED IN 1978.</p>",
